{"name":"Secret Cove","hex":"#68909d","fetched":"2026-10-16","looked":{"definitions":[{"term":"secret","whole":false,"parts":[{"part":"Noun","definitions":["A piece of knowledge that is hidden and intended to be kept hidden. .mw-parser-output .defdate{font-size:smaller}","The key or principle by which something is made clear; the knack."]},{"part":"Verb","definitions":["To make or keep secret.","To hide secretly."]}],"link":"https://en.wiktionary.org/wiki/secret"},{"term":"cove","whole":false,"parts":[{"part":"Noun","definitions":["A hollow in a rock; a cave or cavern. .mw-parser-output .defdate{font-size:smaller}","A concave vault or archway, especially the arch of a ceiling."]},{"part":"Verb","definitions":["To arch over; to build in a hollow concave form; to make in the form of a cove."]}],"link":"https://en.wiktionary.org/wiki/cove"}],"entries":[{"title":"Cove","blocks":[{"text":"A cove is a small bay or coastal inlet. They usually have narrow, restricted entrances, are often circular or oval, and are often situated within a larger bay. Small, narrow, sheltered bays, inlets, tidal creeks, or recesses in a coast are often considered coves."}],"image":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/8/89/McWay_cove_1.jpg/330px-McWay_cove_1.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=api&utm_content=thumbnail","link":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Cove"}],"images":[{"srcset":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/8/89/McWay_cove_1.jpg/500px-McWay_cove_1.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=parser&utm_content=thumbnail 1x, https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/8/89/McWay_cove_1.jpg/1280px-McWay_cove_1.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=parser&utm_content=thumbnail 2x","src":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/8/89/McWay_cove_1.jpg/500px-McWay_cove_1.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=parser&utm_content=thumbnail","alt":"McWay Cove, California, United States","link":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/File%3AMcWay_cove_1.jpg"},{"srcset":"https://upload.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/en/a/a8/Figure_lulworth_formation.png?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=parser&utm_content=thumbnail_unscaled 1x","src":"https://upload.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/en/a/a8/Figure_lulworth_formation.png?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=parser&utm_content=thumbnail_unscaled","alt":"Map showing two examples of how coves form. The rock types are those of Lulworth Cove. In example A, a river breaks through the resistant chalk back rock and limestone, leaving the weak clays to be rapidly eroded. In example B, the sea breaks through the limestone, perhaps by forming a cave, and then erodes the clay away.","link":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/File%3AFigure_lulworth_formation.png"}],"sounds":{"secret":[{"type":"audio/wav","src":"https://upload.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/9/9f/LL-Q1860_%28eng%29-Naomi_Persephone_Amethyst_%28NaomiAmethyst%29-secret.wav?utm_source=en.wiktionary.org&utm_campaign=rest&utm_content=original"},{"type":"audio/mpeg","src":"https://upload.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/transcoded/9/9f/LL-Q1860_%28eng%29-Naomi_Persephone_Amethyst_%28NaomiAmethyst%29-secret.wav/LL-Q1860_%28eng%29-Naomi_Persephone_Amethyst_%28NaomiAmethyst%29-secret.wav.mp3"},{"type":"audio/ogg; codecs=\"vorbis\"","src":"https://upload.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/transcoded/9/9f/LL-Q1860_%28eng%29-Naomi_Persephone_Amethyst_%28NaomiAmethyst%29-secret.wav/LL-Q1860_%28eng%29-Naomi_Persephone_Amethyst_%28NaomiAmethyst%29-secret.wav.ogg"},{"type":"audio/ogg; codecs=\"vorbis\"","src":"https://upload.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/e/e6/En-us-secret.ogg?utm_source=en.wiktionary.org&utm_campaign=rest&utm_content=original"},{"type":"audio/mpeg","src":"https://upload.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/transcoded/e/e6/En-us-secret.ogg/En-us-secret.ogg.mp3"}],"cove":[{"type":"audio/ogg; codecs=\"vorbis\"","src":"https://upload.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/8/86/EN-AU_ck1_cove.ogg?utm_source=en.wikti